- [History and replay](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming/history.md?source=llms.txt): Replay conversation history from the Ably channel before live messages with AI Transport. Join the channel to your own store from a serial, replay from an event, and read history backwards.
- [Streaming](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming.md?source=llms.txt): Stream an agent's output to every connected client over one Ably channel with a transport and a codec, replay history from your own store, and keep the conversation in your own database.
- [Multi-device and fan-out](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming/multi-device.md?source=llms.txt): One agent response reaches every client subscribed to the conversation with Ably AI Transport. Fan-out comes from the channel, so a user can start on a laptop and carry on from a phone.
- [Get started with the Vercel AI SDK](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming/quickstart-vercel.md?source=llms.txt): Build a streaming chat app with the Vercel AI SDK and Ably AI Transport. Responses reach every connected client, and a client that reloads reads the conversation from your own store, then replays what arrived on the channel after it.
- [Write a custom codec](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming/quickstart-wire-codec.md?source=llms.txt): Write a codec with defineCodec for events Ably AI Transport does not ship a codec for, then stream them to every connected client with createTransport.
- [Get started with OpenAI](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming/quickstart-openai.md?source=llms.txt): Build a streaming chat app with the OpenAI Responses API and Ably AI Transport. Responses reach every connected client, and a client that reloads reads the conversation from your own store, then replays what arrived on the channel after it.
- [Reconnection and recovery](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming/reconnection-and-recovery.md?source=llms.txt): AI Transport streams survive connection drops. A brief drop resumes on its own, and after a longer gap a client subscribes again from the last message it received and replays what it missed.
- [Token streaming](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/streaming/token-streaming.md?source=llms.txt): Stream AI-generated output to clients in realtime using AI Transport. Each streamed part of a response is appended to one message, and clients that join later receive the response so far in one delivery.
- [HTTP streaming and AI](https://ably.com/docs/ai-transport/why/http-streaming-and-ai.md?source=llms.txt): Why direct HTTP streaming breaks down for production AI: streams fail on disconnect, sessions do not span devices, clients cannot reach the agent, multi-agent routing is complex, and there are no agent health signals.
